From: mrdidit <mrdidit@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: wcd939x-usbss: add Pocket S2 state recovery

Check the installed Android driver's three USBSS recovery conditions every
15 seconds while awake. On failure, force provider-owned configuration
back to hardware, restore CPLDO and toggle RCO. Keep the Linux regmap
uncached and preserve stable targets across partial configuration failures.
Serialize recovery with measurement and codec-reset transactions, and
cancel work before suspend or removal. Restrict activation to Pocket S2.
Audio-accessory recovery remains excluded without the codec notifier;
explicit teardown remains available. No GPIO reset or fixed audio result
is implied.

The status checks and recovery sequence derive from Qualcomm's GPL-2.0
implementation, cross-checked against the installed S2 module:
https://api.github.com/repos/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm8650/git/blobs/8effe5ea6a8216bf5db182f673ca02b04a1fd14d

